# androidApp/fastlane/.env.example
#
# Copy this file to `androidApp/fastlane/.env` (gitignored) and fill in the
# values. fastlane-dotenv (bundled with fastlane 2.x) loads `.env` automatically
# so anything declared here becomes an env var for every lane in this folder.
#
# In CI we don't use a .env file: the workflow exports these as job-level env
# vars, populated from GitHub Actions Secrets.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Play Console service account (Google Play publishing API)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absolute path to the Play Console service account JSON key file. This is the
# canonical `supply` env var, so both `google_play_track_version_codes` and
# `upload_to_play_store` read it automatically (also fed to the Appfile).
#
# The account must be granted "Release manager" (or at least the ability to
# manage releases + view app info) on the app inside:
#   Play Console → Setup → API access → grant access to the service account.
#
# Munición uses its own dedicated Play Console service account
# (google-play-console-api@municion-95caa.iam.gserviceaccount.com), granted
# access to this app in Play Console. In CI the JSON key is provided via the
# GitHub Actions secret PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON_BASE64.
SUPPLY_JSON_KEY=/absolute/path/to/play-service-account.json
